<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Département</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as department, departments</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A département is an administrative division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> created in 1790 to replace the old provinces with uniform units. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> extended the system to conquered lands and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> after 1848. The term 'department' also describes specialised administrative bodies in other states, such as the departments of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>'s central bureaucracy and the three departments of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/departement.jpg" alt="Département" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nilstilar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:France_d%C3%A9partementale.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
